#
# The milestone the Racket engine currently claims. `just racket-gate` runs the
# cumulative suite M1..M<this number>, and the conform-racket job in CI runs
# `just racket-gate`, so this one digit is what CI holds the engine to.
#
# `0` means no conformance case is claimed yet and the engine's own unit tests
# are the whole gate. `9` means the cumulative suite is the entire built-in
# suite, at which point the gate and `just conform-racket` are the same run.
#
# Advance this in the pull request that makes the milestone pass, never before
# it: the number is a claim about what the engine answers bit for bit. `#` lines
# and blank lines are comments; the file is otherwise one number.
9
